# What must never reach the build context. Phase 33.
#
# This file is the reason `docker build` takes seconds rather than minutes: the
# daemon copies the whole directory before reading the first line of the
# Dockerfile, and `data/` alone is gigabytes of Parquet the image has no use for.

# Secrets. First on purpose. .env holds a live OpenAI key, and a key that enters
# a build context is in the image whether or not any COPY names it.
.env
.envrc

# The medallion layers and the local venv -- the two big ones.
data/
.venv/
logs/

# Everything the image does not run with.
tests/
docs/
corpus/
scripts/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
scratch_*.py
corpus_map.txt
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
CLAUDE.md

# eval/ is NOT ignored: eval/questions.toml and eval/runs/ are copied in
# deliberately, so the run browser works in a container with no key. See the
# Dockerfile's COPY of eval/ for why that is worth ~39 MB.
